# XBD 4.8 File Hierarchy
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XBD.4.8-file-hierarchy.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.8
class      required
says       Only directories have names below them: open(O_CREAT), mkdir(),
           symlink() and mkfifo() with a pathname that goes through a
           regular file, a FIFO or a symbolic link to a regular file fail
           with ENOTDIR (the last component is being created, so no other
           error applies), while the same calls below a directory work.
test       t/001-leaves-have-no-children.c

assertion  XBD.4.8-file-hierarchy.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.8
class      required
says       A file can have several directory entries, in one directory or
           in several: after link() the names give the same device and
           inode, st_nlink counts them, data written through one is read
           through another, and removing names one by one keeps the file
           reachable until the last is gone.
test       t/002-directed-graph.c
